  "title": "Dresden – Elsterwerda – Zossen – Berlin und zurück",
  "notes": "Winter 1913/14, pp. 56-57 (table 13a, Dahme-Uckro, printed under it, is not laid out). Kept rows as in the summer layout: Dresden Hbf, Dresden Wettinerstr., Dresden-Neustadt (in/aus) and Berlin Anh. Bf. Deskew set by hand (-0.45 deg p60, 0.5 deg p61), a compromise between the column rules and the lines of times (p60 is slightly sheared): rows within about 1 px, rules within 1-2 px; heavy box rules (D 65 on p60, D 66 on p61) are split at their middle. p61 has a footnote line under the body (two notes), cropped as 13-fn-p2. On p61 the column of train 316 (c24) is printed 6-10 px lower than its neighbours from r44 down to about r64 (aligned again at the bottom), so it is a panel of its own (p2b) whose row lines round r44 follow its own times; c25 is p2c with the rows of p2."
}
